<title>LATVIA: PARLIAMENT PROLONGS UNIBANKA PROBE.</title>
<headline>PARLIAMENT PROLONGS UNIBANKA PROBE.</headline>
<text>
<p>RIGA, April 24 (Reuiter) - Latvia's parliament on Thursday prolonged its probe into the privatisation of leading bank Unibanka and Savings Bank (Krajbanka) to June 15 from May 1, politicians said.</p>
<p>A parliamentary investigation commission, whose line-up was finalised last week, had asked for more time to prepare its report.</p>
<p>The commission was set up in response to the demands of some opposition MPs, who questioned the circumstances surrounding the sale of state shares in both banks.</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
